{% extends "base.jinja" %}
{% from "person_macro.jinja" import person, handle %}
{# The design system, drawn by itself: every token and component in ds.css,
   rendered by the real stylesheet in whichever theme is on. It is where a
   change to the system is looked at before it reaches a page, and where
   Firefox 56 can be checked in one visit. Unlinked and unindexed; not
   translated, because it is for the people who build the site.

   Everything here is drawn by ds.css's own classes, or by no class at all
   where the system styles the native element. The <style> below only lays
   the samples out; nothing in it may change how a sample looks. #}
{% block title %}Design system | {{ ftl_get_message("brand") }}{% endblock title %}
{% block head %}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
  <style>
    .ds-ref section { margin: 0 0 40px; }
    .ds-ref h2 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: var(--ds-text-xl); }
    .ds-ref h3 { margin: 16px 0 8px; color: var(--ds-muted); font-size: var(--ds-text-m); font-weight: 600; }
    .ds-ref .row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }
    .ds-ref .row > * { margin: 0 12px 12px 0; }
    .ds-ref .row-top { align-items: flex-start; }
    .ds-ref .swatch { width: 132px; }
    .ds-ref .chip { height: 44px; border: 1px solid var(--ds-line); border-radius: var(--ds-radius-s); }
    .ds-ref .chip-text { display: flex; align-items: center; padding: 0 10px; font-size: var(--ds-text-m); }
    .ds-ref .swatch .token { display: block; margin-top: 4px; font-size: var(--ds-text-s); color: var(--ds-muted); }
    .ds-ref .field { width: 280px; }
    .ds-ref .direction p,
    .ds-ref .direction ul { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 0 12px; line-height: 1.55; }
    .ds-ref .direction ul { padding-left: 20px; }
    .ds-ref .direction li + li { margin-top: 6px; }
    .ds-ref .drawing { width: 150px; height: 150px; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--ds-frame); }
    .ds-ref .space { height: 12px; background: var(--ds-accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--ds-accent-line); }
    .ds-ref .box { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 96px; height: 64px; border: 1px solid var(--ds-line-strong); background: var(--ds-surface); font-size: var(--ds-text-s); color: var(--ds-muted); }
    .ds-ref .stack > * + * { margin-top: 8px; }
    .ds-ref .sample-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(260px, 1fr)); grid-gap: 16px; }
    .ds-ref .skeleton-tile { width: 120px; }
  </style>
{% endblock head %}
{% block content %}
  <div class="center ds-ref">
    <h1>Design system</h1>
    <p class="ds-help">Everything in <code>static/ds.css</code>, in the current theme. The painter's Dark button switches it.</p>

    <section class="direction">
      <h2>Direction</h2>
      <p>
        Web 2.0, built on the 90s web. Things have clear edges and vivid colour,
        like the web around 2006, and sit on bones from the oekaki boards a
        decade earlier: the painter's window chrome, graph paper under
        everything, hard pixels. The site should feel like a place where people
        draw, not like a product dashboard that happens to show pictures.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Edges are drawn.</strong> Every box, control and bar has a line
          around it or between it and the next. Nothing is marked out by a
          shadow or a change of shade alone. Rows share one line between them,
          as the toolbar and its notices do.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Colour is vivid.</strong> The ground is NEO's lavender and
          night blue. The cucumber lime means "do this" and appears once per
          view. Orange is for counts, red for what cannot be undone. Use
          saturated colours from the palette rather than neutral greys.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The ground is graph paper.</strong> NEO's 14px grid runs under
          every page, so the site and the painter share one surface. Cards,
          fields and rows sit on it with solid fills and never let it show
          through.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Depth is shallow and hard.</strong> Shadows have no blur: a
          raised control sits on a 1px ledge, and a floating menu or dialog
          casts a 3px offset block. There are no soft, wide glows, and frosted
          glass appears only where the platform uses it, as in the macOS app's
          toolbar.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The 90s stay in the details.</strong> What belongs to drawing
          wears the painter's window: bevel, title bar, grab dots. Drawings keep
          square corners and a frame, and are never smoothed when scaled. Type is
          small and dense (13–14px for the chrome), and corners are rounded only
          a little.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No gradients.</strong> Every fill is one flat colour: no gloss
          on buttons, no fades on bars, no sheen on cards. Depth comes from
          lines and the one small shadow, never from shading. CSS may still
          use <code>linear-gradient()</code> as a tool when both stops are
          the same colour or meet at a hard edge: the grid's 1px lines, a flat
          tint laid over the ground, a slider's filled part. What you see must
          never fade from one colour into another. The one exception is the
          painter itself, whose title bars are NEO's and stay exactly as NEO
          draws them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Native before custom.</strong> Use the browser's own element
          for a job whenever one exists (<code>select</code>,
          <code>details</code>, checkbox, radio, range, <code>fieldset</code>,
          <code>table</code>) and style it here, rather than building a widget
          from <code>div</code>s and script. Native elements work with the
          keyboard, screen readers and the phone's own pickers for free, and
          they survive old engines. Build a custom widget only when no native
          element does the job, or when the Firefox 56 floor rules the
          native one out.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Avoid:</strong> gradients, borderless flat cards,
          grey-on-white minimalism, pill-shaped or heavily rounded boxes, large
          empty margins, and thin light type.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="ds-help">
        It all has to hold in Firefox 56, the engine oekaki users keep for the
        old applets. That is one more reason to use lines and solid fills
        rather than filters and blends.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Colour</h2>
      {% for group, names in [
        ("Ground and surfaces", ["ground", "grid", "surface", "field", "track", "thumb"]),
        ("Ink", ["ink", "muted", "faint"]),
        ("Lines", ["line", "line-strong", "frame"]),
        ("Action and signals", ["accent", "accent-hover", "accent-ink", "accent-line", "focus", "badge", "danger", "danger-hover"]),
        ("States, laid over what is beneath", ["hover", "selected", "press"]),
        ("Loading", ["skeleton", "skeleton-drawing"]),
        ("The painter's window", ["neo-panel", "neo-ink", "neo-text", "neo-light", "neo-shadow", "neo-title", "neo-well"])
      ] %}
        <h3>{{ group }}</h3>
        <div class="row">
          {% for name in names %}
            <div class="swatch">
              <div class="chip" style="background: var(--ds-{{ name }})"></div>
              <code class="token">--ds-{{ name }}</code>
            </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
      <h3>Notices: tint and the ink that reads on it</h3>
      <div class="row">
        {% for level in ["success", "warning", "danger"] %}
          <div class="swatch">
            <div class="chip chip-text" style="background: var(--ds-{{ level }}-surface); color: var(--ds-{{ level }}-text)">{{ level | capitalize }}</div>
            <code class="token">--ds-{{ level }}-*</code>
          </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Type</h2>
      {% for size in ["2xl", "xl", "l", "base", "m", "s", "xs"] %}
        <div style="font-size: var(--ds-text-{{ size }})">--ds-text-{{ size }} · 오이카페 OEEEカフェ Oeee Cafe</div>
      {% endfor %}
      <h3>Headings and text</h3>
      <div class="ds-card stack">
        <h1 style="margin: 0">Heading one · 그림 게시판</h1>
        <h2 style="margin: 0">Heading two · お絵かき</h2>
        <h3 style="margin: 0; color: var(--ds-ink); font-size: var(--ds-text-l)">Heading three</h3>
        <p style="margin: 0">Body text is the page's own weight. A <a href="#">link in a sentence</a> is underlined; <strong>strong</strong> and <em>emphasis</em> read as they do anywhere. <mark>Marked text</mark> for a search's match.</p>
        <p class="ds-help" style="margin: 0">Help text, under a field or beside a count.</p>
        <p style="margin: 0">Inline <code>code</code>, and keys: <kbd>G</kbd> then <kbd>R</kbd>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Space, corners and depth</h2>
      <h3>Space: a 4px scale</h3>
      <div class="stack">
        {% for step in range(1, 7) %}
          <div class="row" style="margin: 0"><div class="space" style="width: var(--ds-space-{{ step }})"></div><code class="token">--ds-space-{{ step }}</code></div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      <h3>Corners and shadows</h3>
      <div class="row">
        <div class="box" style="border-radius: var(--ds-radius-s)">radius-s</div>
        <div class="box" style="border-radius: var(--ds-radius-m)">radius-m</div>
        <div class="box" style="border-radius: var(--ds-radius-m); box-shadow: var(--ds-shadow-raise)">shadow-raise</div>
        <div class="box" style="border-radius: var(--ds-radius-m); box-shadow: var(--ds-shadow-menu)">shadow-menu</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Buttons</h2>
      <div class="row">
        <button class="ds-button ds-button-primary" type="button">Primary</button>
        <button class="ds-button" type="button">Secondary</button>
        <button class="ds-button ds-button-quiet" type="button">Quiet</button>
        <button class="ds-button ds-button-danger" type="button">Delete</button>
        <button class="ds-button" type="button" disabled>Disabled</button>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <button class="ds-button ds-button-small ds-button-primary" type="button">Small primary</button>
        <button class="ds-button ds-button-small" type="button">Small</button>
        <button class="ds-button ds-button-small ds-button-quiet" type="button">Small quiet</button>
        <a class="ds-button" href="#">A link as a button</a>
      </div>
      <h3>Native, with no class</h3>
      <div class="row">
        <button type="button">Button</button>
        <input type="submit" value="Submit" />
        <input type="reset" value="Reset" />
        <button type="button" disabled>Disabled</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Fields</h2>
      <div class="row row-top">
        <label class="field">
          <span class="ds-label">Title</span>
          <input class="ds-input" type="text" placeholder="Untitled" style="width: 100%" />
          <span class="ds-help">Shown above the drawing.</span>
        </label>
        <label class="field">
          <span class="ds-label">Disabled</span>
          <input class="ds-input" type="text" value="Cannot be changed" disabled style="width: 100%" />
        </label>
      </div>
      <label>
        <span class="ds-label">Description</span>
        <textarea class="ds-textarea" rows="3" style="width: 100%">날다람지</textarea>
      </label>
      <h3>Native, with no class</h3>
      <div class="row row-top">
        {% for type, label, value in [("text", "Text", "A plain input"), ("email", "Email", "tandemaus@oeee.cafe"), ("password", "Password", "hunter22"), ("search", "Search", "#oekaki"), ("number", "Number", "12"), ("url", "Link", "https://oeee.cafe"), ("tel", "Phone", ""), ("date", "Date", "2026-09-23"), ("time", "Time", "14:30")] %}
          <label class="field">
            <span class="ds-label">{{ label }}</span>
            <input type="{{ type }}" value="{{ value }}" style="width: 100%" />
          </label>
        {% endfor %}
        <label class="field">
          <span class="ds-label">File</span>
          <input type="file" />
        </label>
        <label class="field">
          <span class="ds-label">Colour</span>
          <input type="color" value="#c4ee62" />
        </label>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Drop-downs</h2>
      <div class="row row-top">
        <select class="ds-select" aria-label="Community">
          <option>Pokémon</option>
          <option>페르소나!!</option>
          <option>오이카페 모에화</option>
        </select>
        <select aria-label="Visibility">
          <option>Public</option>
          <option>Unlisted</option>
          <option>Private</option>
        </select>
        <select aria-label="Canvas">
          <optgroup label="Square">
            <option>300 × 300</option>
            <option>400 × 400</option>
          </optgroup>
          <optgroup label="Wide">
            <option>400 × 300</option>
            <option>600 × 400</option>
          </optgroup>
        </select>
        <select class="ds-select" aria-label="Disabled" disabled>
          <option>Disabled</option>
        </select>
        <select multiple size="4" aria-label="Tags">
          <option selected>oekaki</option>
          <option>pixel</option>
          <option selected>cucumber</option>
          <option>sketch</option>
          <option>relay</option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Choices</h2>
      <div class="row">
        <label><input type="checkbox" checked /> Allow relays</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Sensitive</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" class="ds-indeterminate" /> Some</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" checked disabled /> Locked</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="ref-radio" checked /> Public</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="ref-radio" /> Private</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="ref-radio" disabled /> Disabled</label>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <label><input type="range" min="1" max="12" value="6" aria-label="Size" /></label>
        <div class="ds-segmented" role="group" aria-label="Whose drawings">
          <button type="button" aria-pressed="true">Everyone</button>
          <button type="button" aria-pressed="false">Following</button>
          <button type="button" aria-pressed="false">Mine</button>
        </div>
        <span class="ds-badge">3</span>
        <span class="ds-badge">128</span>
      </div>
      <script>
        document.querySelectorAll(".ds-indeterminate").forEach(function (box) { box.indeterminate = true; });
      </script>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Forms</h2>
      <p class="ds-help">A plain <code>fieldset</code> is a card and its <code>legend</code> the title; the submit is the lime one.</p>
      <form onsubmit="return false">
        <fieldset>
          <legend>Profile</legend>
          <p>
            <label for="ref-name">Display name</label>
            <input id="ref-name" type="text" value="날다람지" />
          </p>
          <p>
            <label for="ref-bio">Bio</label>
            <textarea id="ref-bio" rows="2">Draws cucumbers.</textarea>
          </p>
          <p>
            <input id="ref-public" type="checkbox" checked />
            <label for="ref-public">Show my drawings on the home page</label>
          </p>
          <div class="form-actions">
            <button type="submit">Save</button>
            <button type="button" class="ds-button">Cancel</button>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      </form>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Native elements</h2>
      <p class="ds-help">Elements the browser already knows how to do, styled rather than rebuilt.</p>
      <div class="sample-grid">
        <div class="stack">
          <details>
            <summary>What is oekaki?</summary>
            <p>Drawing in the browser, on a small canvas, with a replay of every stroke.</p>
          </details>
          <details open>
            <summary>An open disclosure</summary>
            <p>Opened by default with the <code>open</code> attribute.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
        <div class="stack">
          <label class="ds-label" for="ref-progress">Uploading</label>
          <progress id="ref-progress" value="62" max="100">62%</progress>
          <label class="ds-label" for="ref-meter">Storage</label>
          <meter id="ref-meter" value="0.7" low="0.5" high="0.9" optimum="0.2">70%</meter>
        </div>
        <div class="stack">
          <blockquote>A replay that renders differently from the canvas it was recorded on is the worst failure this codebase can produce.</blockquote>
          <hr />
          <pre>ssh mini 'zsh -l -c deploy.sh'</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3>Table</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>User</th><th>Drawings</th><th>Joined</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>날다람지</td><td>128</td><td>2024-03-02</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tandemaus</td><td>41</td><td>2025-11-19</td></tr>
          <tr><td>きゅうり</td><td>7</td><td>2026-09-01</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Notices</h2>
      <p class="ds-help">Flash messages and the htmx error banner, as rows of the header. The level is the colour; Info and Debug are plain, with the accent's dot.</p>
      <ul class="ds-notices" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ds-line)">
        {% for level, text in [("info", "Your drawing is saved as a draft."), ("success", "Welcome, 날다람지!"), ("warning", "This community is about to be archived."), ("error", "The passwords did not match. 비밀번호가 일치하지 않습니다.")] %}
          <li class="ds-notice ds-notice-{{ level }}">
            <span class="ds-notice-body">{{ text }}</span>
            {% include "notice_close.jinja" %}
          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Surfaces</h2>
      <div class="row row-top">
        <div class="ds-card" style="width: 280px">
          <strong>A card</strong>
          <p class="ds-help">Settings groups, forms, anything that is a box on the ground.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ds-card ds-stack" style="width: 280px">
          <strong>A card that is a stack</strong>
          <p class="ds-help"><code>.ds-stack</code> drops its children's own margins and puts one gap between each.</p>
          <div><button type="button" class="ds-button">A row of buttons</button></div>
          <p class="ds-help">Whatever comes next is the same distance away.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ds-window" style="width: 280px">
          <div class="ds-window-title">Replay</div>
          <div class="ds-window-body">What belongs to drawing wears the painter's chrome.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="drawing" aria-label="A drawing's frame"></div>
      </div>
      <h3>An alert, as hx-confirm asks through it</h3>
      <div class="ds-modal-panel ds-alert-panel">
        <p class="ds-alert-message">Delete this drawing? Its replay goes with it.</p>
        <div class="ds-alert-actions">
          <button type="button" class="ds-button">Cancel</button>
          <button type="button" class="ds-button ds-button-danger">Delete</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>People</h2>
      <p class="ds-help"><code>person()</code> in person_macro.jinja: the name, then the handle as a pill. Everyone's pill is a ring; a supporter's is the accent, with their mark inside. Someone from here is <code>@login_name</code>; someone from another server keeps <code>@name@their.host</code>. <code>handle()</code> is the pill alone, for a line that says more after it.</p>
      <div class="ds-stack">
        <div>{{ person("Tandemaus", "#", login_name="tandemaus") }}</div>
        <div>{{ person("Tandemaus", "#", login_name="tandemaus", supporters={"tandemaus": "steam"}) }}</div>
        <div>{{ person("Someone far", "#", actor_handle="@someone@example.social", external=true) }}</div>
        <div>{{ handle("tandemaus") }} · 3 days ago</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Waiting</h2>
      <div class="row row-top">
        <div class="skeleton-tile">
          <div class="ds-skeleton-square"></div>
          <span class="ds-skeleton-bar ds-skeleton-gap" style="width: 80%; height: 12px"></span>
          <span class="ds-skeleton-bar ds-skeleton-gap" style="width: 50%; height: 12px"></span>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 240px">
          <span class="ds-skeleton-bar" style="width: 70%; height: 20px"></span>
          <span class="ds-skeleton-bar ds-skeleton-gap-l" style="height: 12px"></span>
          <span class="ds-skeleton-bar ds-skeleton-gap" style="height: 12px"></span>
          <span class="ds-skeleton-bar ds-skeleton-gap" style="width: 60%; height: 12px"></span>
        </div>
        <span class="ds-spinner">Loading</span>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
{% endblock content %}
